<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria offers two treasury paper issues Sept 13.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria offers two treasury paper issues Sept 13.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer a T-bill and a T-note issue with a total par of 4.0 billion levs, both dated September 19, at two auctions on Friday, the central bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The T-bill issue is a discount one with maturity of 28 days.</p>
<p>The T-note issue is a floater coupon one and was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry, the BNB said in a statement.</p>
<p>Its coupon is set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at annual 108 percent.</p>
<p> Issue number	BG2032596129	 BG3016296025</p>
<p> Type		  Floater coupon     Discount</p>
<p> Par value	   200 million levs	 3.8 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	Sept 13, 1996	Sept 13, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	  Sept 19, 1996	Sept 19, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date     Sept 17, 1998	Oct 17, 1996</p>
<p>Interest payments March 20, 1997</p>
<p>			 Sept 18, 1997</p>
<p>			 March 19, 1998</p>
<p>			 Sept 17, 1998</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
